rf.ts\",\n      \"line\": 6,\n      \"description\": \"Token Caching/Expiry: CSRF token is cached indefinitely in memory. If token expires on server, client won't fetch a new one until reconnect or refresh. Implement token refresh logic or shorter cache TTL.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"next.config.ts\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"description\": \"Environment Exposure: `A0_URL` with fallback to `localhost:5000` means dev endpoint could leak into production if env var not set. Explicitly require env var in production: `process.env.A0_URL || (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' ? throw new Error(...) : 'http://localhost:5000')`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/lib/socket-client.ts\",\n      \"line\": 28,\n      \"description\": \"Auth Callback: On every reconnect, CSRF token is re-fetched. While this improves freshness, the old cached token in memory could conflict. Clear old token before refetch or use socket state to track auth state.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 52,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"**CRITICAL:** Escape or sanitize all log content before rendering. Add a utility function `escapeHtml()` or use a React library like `react-markdown` with `sanitizeHtml` plugin. For `use-chat.ts`, `use-action-cards.ts`, and `use-expo-stream.ts`, wrap content in `<pre>` or sanitized markdown renderer.\",\n    \"Use `react-markdown` with `rehype-sanitize` for any rich text from logs. Configure to allow only safe HTML tags (no scripts, iframes, event handlers).\",\n    \"Replace manual URL construction in `use-workspace.ts` with `URLSearchParams`: `new URLSearchParams({ location_id: locationId }).toString()`.\",\n    \"Implement CSRF token refresh: add expiry check and refresh logic before each request. Store expiry time alongside token.\",\n    \"Move CSRF token storage to HttpOnly cookie only (backend-set). If frontend caching is needed, use sessionStorage + clear on logout.\",\n    \"Add